UID:10057822-1785639600-1785725999@livemusicasheville.com
SUMMARY:TONIGHT | Oteil & Friends featuring Steve Kimock\, Jason Crosby\, Johnny Kimock\, Tom Guarna\, & Lamar Williams\, Jr. w/sg Road to Roots
DESCRIPTION:Sunday\, August 2  •  4:30 pm – 10:00 pm | From $64.46 Event Details and Tickets \nTwo-time Grammy Award–winning bassist Oteil Burbridge has spent more than three decades touring and recording at the highest level of modern music. Most recently known for his role in Dead & Company\, Oteil joined Bob Weir\, Bill Kreutzmann\, and Mickey Hart alongside John Mayer for ten major tours\, helping carry forward the Grateful Dead legacy for a new generation.A founding member of the early ’90s Southern jazz-fusion group Col. Bruce Hampton & the Aquarium Rescue Unit\, Oteil later became the longest-tenured bassist in the history of The Allman Brothers Band. In recognition of his 15-year tenure with the group\, he received a Grammy Lifetime Achievement Award in 2012.Oteil continues to tour extensively with Oteil & Friends\, his ever-evolving project featuring a rotating lineup of world-class musicians including Melvin Seals\, Jason Crosby\, Jeff Chimenti\, Steve Kimock\, and more. He is also a member of The Toy Factory Project\, led by original Marshall Tucker Band drummer Paul T. Riddle\, honoring the legacy of guitarist Toy Caldwell and featuring collaborators such as Marcus King\, Charlie Starr\, and Josh Shilling. \n\nRoad to Roots will be opening on the indoor stage for Oteil & Friends this Sunday.\n\n\nPresented by Melody Trucks and Melissa McKinney Music\, Road to Roots brings together alumni of @rootsrockrevival\, the music camp co-founded by @oteil_burbridge and the late Butch Trucks to mentor the next generation of musicians.\n\n\nFeaturing Strictly Liquid with special guests Elijah Good\, Tom Fenton\, Jacob Good\, and Dylan Fenton\, this special set celebrates the community that’s grown from Roots Rock Revival and makes for a fitting start to an amazing day of music.\n\n  \nFrench Broad River Brewery is more than just a place to enjoy a drink—it’s a community hub where great beer\, delicious pizza\, live music\, and good times come together. Just minutes from the Biltmore Estate & Downtown\, our taproom is a gathering spot for locals and visitors alike. We regularly host live music and entertainment in our taproom\, making French Broad River Brewery a lively hub of local activity. From bluegrass to reggae\, there’s always something happening. Check out our Events Page to see what’s coming up next! \nNo brewery experience is complete without great food. That’s why we offer French Broad River Pizza\, serving up hot\, hand-tossed pizzas made to order. Whether you’re here for a quick slice or a full meal\, our pizza perfectly complements our craft beers and the lively atmosphere of our taproom. frenchbroadbrewery.com/pizza
URL:https://livemusicasheville.com/calendar/oteil-friends-featuring-steve-kimock-jason-crosby-johnny-kimock-tom-guarna-lamar-williams-jr/
LOCATION:French Broad River Brewery\, 101 Fairview Rd\, Asheville\, NC\, United States
CATEGORIES:Asheville Area,Live Music
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://livemusicasheville.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/04/759330418_1636770908450239_869278489655886392_n-e1785338794958.jpg
GEO:35.5662722;-82.5374054
X-APPLE-STRUCTURED-LOCATION;VALUE=URI;X-ADDRESS=French Broad River Brewery 101 Fairview Rd Asheville NC United States;X-APPLE-RADIUS=500;X-TITLE=101 Fairview Rd:geo:-82.5374054,35.5662722
END:VEVENT
